### Orchestrator Microservice API - Sample Requests
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension or IntelliJ HTTP Client

### IMPORTANT: Make sure all microservices are running before testing:
### - Inventory Service: http://localhost:8080
### - Payment Service: http://localhost:8081
### - Shipping Service: http://localhost:8082
### - Orchestrator Service: http://localhost:8083

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8083

### The orchestrator fills unit prices from the stock check, so requests need not
### send prices. Flow: stock -> (production if low) -> quote -> payment (retry x2) -> confirm.

### ========================================
### ORDER SCENARIOS
### ========================================

### SCENARIO 1: Successful order - MacBook Neo x3 from Colombo -> Colombo
### Grand total ~1,050,675 LKR (below step-up threshold) => COMPLETED
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "customerId": "CUST-001",
    "branchId": "BRANCH-COL",
    "items": [
        { "itemId": "MACBOOK-NEO-001", "quantity": 3 }
    ],
    "shippingAddress": {
        "line1": "42 Galle Road",
        "city": "Colombo",
        "area": "Colombo 03",
        "country": "Sri Lanka"
    },
    "paymentDetails": { "paymentMethod": "CARD", "currency": "LKR" }
}

###

### SCENARIO 2: Out of stock - MacBook Air from Colombo (0 units) => INSUFFICIENT_STOCK
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "customerId": "CUST-002",
    "branchId": "BRANCH-COL",
    "items": [
        { "itemId": "MACBOOK-AIR-001", "quantity": 1 }
    ],
    "shippingAddress": {
        "line1": "42 Galle Road",
        "city": "Colombo",
        "area": "Colombo 03",
        "country": "Sri Lanka"
    },
    "paymentDetails": { "paymentMethod": "CARD", "currency": "LKR" }
}

###

